INTERPRETATION (separated from the numbers above)
  The network σ head (aleatoric) is spatially almost constant: std 0.0012
  around 0.350, i.e. pinned at sigma_target. It cannot flag the y ≈ −3 km
  stripe. corr(aleatoric, spread) ≈ 0, so the head does not track disagreement.
  corr(bundle.sigma, spread) is high only because bundle.sigma = hypot(head, spread)
  and the head is flat — that correlation is algebraic, not a second measurement.

  At y ≈ −3 km, combined σ is slightly below the rest of the model and
  ensemble spread is well below it. Both say 'I am sure' on the column
  that hosts the depth-wrong vertical conductor. They do not diverge:
  members agree with each other on the wrong conductor. |μ−truth| in the
  column is higher than the rest, so confidence and error anti-align here.
  Single-run numbers; not a 3-seed claim. TRAIN_SEED=2026, nmembers=5.
  This is prior-stage fusion (warm start), not joint inversion.
